It is necessary to put liboceandirect.so into your library path to run any programs against this driver. It should suffice to do this within the OceanDirect root directory (where this {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK  \\l "AAAAAAABCI" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 README.txt}}} is) for testing:\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid     $ export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$PWD/lib"\par
}
\par
Alternately, liboceandirect.so could be installed into a system library directory like /usr/local/lib that ld.so knows about.\par
Test programs in the 'test' directory should be built alongside OceanDirect and can be used as starting points for new development. As long as the LD_LIBRARY_PATH above is properly defined, these should work. If they do not, then they may need to be updated to reflect the current state of the driver API.\par}
\par}
