{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Set the width of the boxcar smoothing to be applied to the returned spectrum. When this value is set greater than 0, boxcar smoothing (a moving average) is applied to the spectrum returned by getFormattedSpectrum (or getRawSpectrumWithMetadata). The width specified is the number of pixels either side of the central pixel of the average i.e. if the result of this function is n, the "full width" of the smoothing is 2*n+1.\par
Setting this value to 0 turns off the boxcar smoothing. \par
